WEBVTT

1
00:04:04.708 --> 00:04:05.792
What is your profession?

2
00:04:08.333 --> 00:04:09.625
What is your job?

3
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.875
Sir, we…

4
00:04:14.542 --> 00:04:15.542
Helpers.

5
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.125
Company work…

6
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.292
Helpers.

7
00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:22.000
Have you both come together?

8
00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:24.667
Are you both together?

9
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:25.833
Helpers.

10
00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:41.375
I'm so sorry.

11
00:04:47.792 --> 00:04:49.583
- What's your name?
- Chaminda.

12
00:04:49.833 --> 00:04:50.833
Chaminda?

13
00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:52.792
Chaminda.

14
00:04:52.875 --> 00:04:53.875
Passport?

15
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:57.559
Brother, I can't find our names
on any of these placards.

16
00:04:57.583 --> 00:05:00.463
Look, they're taking many people
and verifying their names and documents.

17
00:05:00.708 --> 00:05:01.625
Passport?

18
00:05:01.708 --> 00:05:03.958
Brother, which flight did you arrive on?

19
00:05:04.042 --> 00:05:05.083
No.

20
00:05:05.833 --> 00:05:07.333
- What did he ask?
- No idea.

21
00:05:07.708 --> 00:05:09.458
- What did you say?
- "No."

22
00:05:09.625 --> 00:05:10.708
"I don't know."

23
00:05:12.542 --> 00:05:14.917
Go and ask them
if our names are on their list.

24
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Me?

25
00:05:16.958 --> 00:05:18.708
They won't understand if I ask them.

26
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:21.750
Hey, they are leaving!

27
00:05:22.042 --> 00:05:23.292
Go! Hurry up!

28
00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:28.833
- Have you come from Bombay?
- Sri Lanka.

29
00:05:28.917 --> 00:05:30.277
Which company are you working for?

30
00:05:33.583 --> 00:05:34.917
They are from Sri Lanka.

31
00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.292
Allah!

32
00:05:39.042 --> 00:05:40.625
Whom do we ask now?

33
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.268
If it's an office number,
there's no way you can reach them.

34
00:05:57.292 --> 00:05:59.083
Today is Friday,
and it's a holiday here.

35
00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:02.292
Do you have any other phone number?

36
00:06:02.417 --> 00:06:03.817
A residence number or pager number?

37
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.375
Due to the anxiety of boarding the plane,
I forgot to ask about all that.

38
00:06:07.458 --> 00:06:09.458
The phone is ringing,
but no one is answering.

39
00:06:09.542 --> 00:06:10.833
It might be an office number.

40
00:06:12.042 --> 00:06:13.333
This is so foolish!

41
00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:15.184
We should have asked the agent in Bombay

42
00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.208
for the contact number
of the person picking us up.

43
00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:19.917
Well, fantastic timing!

44
00:06:20.083 --> 00:06:22.042
You don't have to worry.
The Kafeel will come.

45
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:23.417
You have visas, right?

46
00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.542
He must be stuck in traffic
because it's a holiday.

47
00:06:34.375 --> 00:06:35.417
Brother…

48
00:06:35.542 --> 00:06:38.708
I think everyone who came with us
has left. I can't see anyone here.

49
00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.792
Would they have left
without recognizing us?

50
00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.125
Brother, it's 8:30 p.m.

51
00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.042
My mother must be getting really worried.

52
00:06:56.542 --> 00:06:58.942
Shouldn't we inform them that
we've arrived here from Bombay?

53
00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:00.500
It's late in the night.

54
00:07:01.708 --> 00:07:02.708
But how?

55
00:07:03.458 --> 00:07:04.958
The evening prayer just ended.

56
00:07:06.333 --> 00:07:09.417
Oh! There's a time zone difference
between here and India, right?

57
00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:16.167
Did you notice how happy Shashi was
when I gave him my watch?

58
00:07:17.292 --> 00:07:18.292
Poor fellow.

59
00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.434
He has been waiting for so long
in Bombay to come to the Middle East,

60
00:07:21.458 --> 00:07:22.667
just like us.

61
00:07:27.375 --> 00:07:28.583
- Hakim!
- Yes?

62
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:30.875
I think he's our man.

63
00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.250
It seems like he's looking for someone.

64
00:07:33.375 --> 00:07:34.458
Shall we go and ask him?

65
00:07:35.083 --> 00:07:36.375
Go and ask him in English.

66
00:07:36.708 --> 00:07:38.083
No, I don't think that would work.

67
00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:39.833
He's coming here.

68
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.750
Is your name Abdullah?

69
00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:46.750
And you?

70
00:07:47.083 --> 00:07:48.083
What is your name?

71
00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:51.367
Tell him that we have come here
on Sreekumar sir's visa.

72
00:07:52.083 --> 00:07:53.875
I'm asking for your name!
Can't you hear me?

73
00:07:55.833 --> 00:07:57.042
Where have you come from?

74
00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.875
Who is your Kafeel?

75
00:08:02.875 --> 00:08:03.916
Don't you have any brains?

76
00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.125
Oh, God!

77
00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.000
Such a disaster!

78
00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:14.875
What did he say?

79
00:08:14.958 --> 00:08:17.333
I have no idea.
All I understood was "Abdullah".

80
00:08:17.833 --> 00:08:19.583
He was stinking, right?

81
00:08:20.917 --> 00:08:23.500
Well, didn't you joke before

82
00:08:23.583 --> 00:08:26.458
that attar and perfumes are made
from the sweat and urine of Arabs?

83
00:08:27.333 --> 00:08:28.417
I wasn't joking.

84
00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:30.333
The real Arabs are like that.

85
00:08:30.792 --> 00:08:32.750
They bathe using water infused with attar.

86
00:08:32.958 --> 00:08:36.167
This guy seems like a rugged Arab
who hasn't bathed in ages!

87
00:08:37.708 --> 00:08:39.393
Anyway, the Kafeels are
still turning up, right?

88
00:08:39.417 --> 00:08:40.417
What?

89
00:08:41.542 --> 00:08:42.542
Kafeel.

90
00:08:43.042 --> 00:08:45.143
That's the first Arab word
I learned after coming here.

91
00:08:45.167 --> 00:08:46.167
What does it mean?

92
00:08:46.958 --> 00:08:48.083
It means…

93
00:08:48.708 --> 00:08:49.708
Boss.

94
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.000
Our man.

95
00:08:51.292 --> 00:08:52.292
Our employer.

96
00:08:52.417 --> 00:08:53.417
Sponsor.

97
00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:54.833
Kafeel!

98
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.667
I wonder where our Kafeel is.

99
00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:04.833
Give me your passport.

100
00:09:10.042 --> 00:09:11.250
Give me your passport too.

101
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.250
Brother, he's our Kafeel. Let's go.

102
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.792
Come on, let's hurry!
It's already late.

103
00:09:30.542 --> 00:09:32.792
I don't understand what
these guys are saying.

104
00:09:36.458 --> 00:09:38.125
Don't you want to go quickly?

105
00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:39.750
Come on! Get inside!

106
00:09:39.833 --> 00:09:42.042
Get in the vehicle! Come on!

107
00:09:42.583 --> 00:09:43.917
-Oh, no!
- What is this?

108
00:09:45.208 --> 00:09:47.958
Get inside, quick! Come on!

109
00:09:50.458 --> 00:09:52.042
These guys are driving me crazy!

110
00:09:53.167 --> 00:09:55.750
Sir… may I get some water to drink?

111
00:09:56.542 --> 00:09:58.083
What are you murmuring?

112
00:09:59.625 --> 00:10:00.667
Water.

113
00:10:00.792 --> 00:10:01.917
Don't you understand?

114
00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.750
Go and sit at the back. Go!

115
00:10:06.667 --> 00:10:09.083
Get into the vehicle. Come on.
Don't waste time.

116
00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.000
What are you doing? Not here!

117
00:10:14.083 --> 00:10:15.417
Didn't I ask you to go there?

118
00:10:15.792 --> 00:10:17.625
Go and sit at the back.

119
00:10:18.208 --> 00:10:19.208
Go!

120
00:10:19.458 --> 00:10:20.458
Brother!

121
00:10:20.833 --> 00:10:22.417
Why is he shouting so much?

122
00:10:23.542 --> 00:10:25.182
He wouldn't have
understood what we asked.

123
00:10:25.333 --> 00:10:27.958
Well, we've come here as
company helpers, right?

124
00:10:28.333 --> 00:10:29.851
And they are taking us in this vehicle?

125
00:10:29.875 --> 00:10:32.542
Didn't you see?
Those Sri Lankans were taken in an AC bus.

126
00:10:33.792 --> 00:10:34.792
You get in.

127
00:10:35.917 --> 00:10:37.042
May God protect us.

128
00:10:47.292 --> 00:10:48.375
Brother, look!

129
00:10:48.542 --> 00:10:49.542
It's a tunnel.

130
00:10:51.208 --> 00:10:53.042
Vehicles are passing
above this tunnel.

131
00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.375
Brother! It's even better
to stand and watch!

132
00:11:02.542 --> 00:11:03.542
Come on!

133
00:11:21.792 --> 00:11:23.292
It's really late, Hakim.

134
00:11:23.917 --> 00:11:25.997
We haven't been able to contact
anyone back home yet.

135
00:11:27.708 --> 00:11:29.875
Oh, I completely forgot about that!

136
00:11:30.167 --> 00:11:32.417
We should stop somewhere
and make those calls.

137
00:11:32.917 --> 00:11:34.333
- Kafeel!
- No!

138
00:11:34.708 --> 00:11:36.958
Let's make those calls
once we get to our room.

139
00:11:37.458 --> 00:11:39.375
Brother, it's already past 10:00 p.m.

140
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.042
My mother must be terrified.

141
00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.500
Kafeel!

142
00:11:45.542 --> 00:11:48.250
I need to make a call home.
Could you please stop the vehicle?

143
00:11:48.333 --> 00:11:49.917
Why are you blabbering?

144
00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.500
Go! Go back!

145
00:11:51.625 --> 00:11:52.917
- But…
- The cops will catch you!

146
00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:55.000
You can stop at a phone booth.

147
00:11:55.458 --> 00:11:57.458
Can't you understand?
Go back and sit!

148
00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.500
How do I make him understand?

149
00:11:59.583 --> 00:12:01.083
- Brother!
- Yes!

150
00:12:01.208 --> 00:12:02.625
Where are you taking them?

151
00:12:02.792 --> 00:12:03.875
To the market?

152
00:12:04.708 --> 00:12:06.833
- Wishing you well!
- Wishing you the best!

153
00:12:06.917 --> 00:12:08.125
May God bless you!

154
00:13:16.958 --> 00:13:17.958
Where are we?

155
00:13:18.125 --> 00:13:19.125
Have we reached?

156
00:13:22.458 --> 00:13:23.458
Abu Khaled!

157
00:13:24.167 --> 00:13:25.167
Abu Khaled!

158
00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:27.750
Get down.

159
00:13:29.458 --> 00:13:31.339
I asked you to get down.
This is your workplace.

160
00:13:32.583 --> 00:13:34.125
Can't you hear me?

161
00:13:36.583 --> 00:13:37.667
What's going on?

162
00:13:38.542 --> 00:13:39.542
Get down.

163
00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.417
Get down.

164
00:13:43.375 --> 00:13:44.542
No. You stay here.

165
00:13:44.625 --> 00:13:45.708
You come with me.

166
00:13:49.542 --> 00:13:51.042
- Hey, brother!
- Sir!

167
00:13:52.375 --> 00:13:53.375
Sir!

168
00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.167
We assumed our accommodation
would be in town.

169
00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:58.208
We need to call our families.

170
00:13:58.792 --> 00:14:00.708
- Phone call...
- You're blabbering too much!

171
00:14:01.167 --> 00:14:02.833
Go! Go back to the vehicle!

172
00:14:03.042 --> 00:14:05.333
Hakim, try to make
him understand somehow.

173
00:14:05.458 --> 00:14:07.625
Isn't he asking me
to get back into the vehicle?

174
00:14:08.708 --> 00:14:10.976
Don't you dare talk too much!
Go and get into the vehicle.

175
00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.208
Don't be a pain in the neck! Go!

176
00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.583
Kafeel, we are together…

177
00:14:16.333 --> 00:14:17.667
Open your mouth
and say something!

178
00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:18.750
Hello!

179
00:14:18.917 --> 00:14:21.292
Hello, Abu Khaled!
Why have you locked the gate?

180
00:14:21.542 --> 00:14:23.000
Due to the threat of wild animals.

181
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.042
Listen, Abu Khaled.

182
00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.208
Let this boy stay here.

183
00:14:28.417 --> 00:14:30.250
- Brother…
- I'll contact you tomorrow.

184
00:14:30.375 --> 00:14:32.917
Kiddo, whether it's English or Hindi,

185
00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.750
just convey it in a language
you're familiar with.

186
00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:37.167
How else can we…

187
00:14:37.875 --> 00:14:38.917
Go!

188
00:14:41.167 --> 00:14:43.250
Sir, Kafeel…

189
00:14:43.583 --> 00:14:45.833
we've come on the same company's visa.

190
00:14:46.667 --> 00:14:47.667
Helpers.

191
00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:49.667
We stay together.

192
00:14:49.833 --> 00:14:51.042
Shut up!
Go back!

193
00:14:51.333 --> 00:14:52.625
Go back!
Quick!

194
00:14:53.333 --> 00:14:55.375
Kafeel, we are together.

195
00:14:55.458 --> 00:14:56.667
One room…

196
00:14:56.875 --> 00:14:58.042
You move away.

197
00:14:58.167 --> 00:15:00.167
- Come on! Take him!
- Brother!

198
00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.250
- Hakim!
- Let go of me!

199
00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:02.208
Out!

200
00:15:02.292 --> 00:15:04.667
- We have come together!
- Hey! Go back, I say!

201
00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:06.833
- Brother! Brother!
- Go back, I say!

202
00:15:06.917 --> 00:15:08.667
- Listen to me!
- Why are you hitting me?

203
00:15:08.917 --> 00:15:10.250
Go back, I say!

204
00:15:10.417 --> 00:15:13.000
- Brother!
- Be careful with him!

205
00:15:13.667 --> 00:15:15.167
- Don't let go of him!
- Brother!

206
00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:18.125
- Where are you going? Come on!
- No…

207
00:15:18.208 --> 00:15:19.708
We have come together!

208
00:15:19.875 --> 00:15:22.375
- Brother!
- Where are you going? Come back!

209
00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.833
- Hakim!
- Come on!

210
00:15:24.667 --> 00:15:26.542
- Don't go!
- Stop the vehicle!

211
00:15:26.667 --> 00:15:28.208
- Don't go, Brother!
- Stop it!

212
00:15:28.292 --> 00:15:29.167
Don't go!

213
00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:30.708
- Brother!
- Hakim!

214
00:15:30.792 --> 00:15:31.792
Brother!

215
00:16:18.458 --> 00:16:20.167
Praise be to Allah!

216
00:16:23.333 --> 00:16:24.375
Get off.

217
00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.542
Come on, get off.

218
00:16:33.292 --> 00:16:34.417
Get down quickly.

219
00:16:36.917 --> 00:16:38.375
Come on!
Get down quickly!

220
00:16:52.458 --> 00:16:54.708
Where are you, Jaseer?
Are you sleeping?

221
00:16:55.125 --> 00:16:58.625
No, Uncle. I'm not sleeping.
I'm here.

222
00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:00.708
Yes, yes.
I saw you.

223
00:17:03.458 --> 00:17:04.750
Hello! How are you doing?

224
00:17:04.833 --> 00:17:07.000
Doing great, by God's grace.

225
00:17:07.083 --> 00:17:09.458
- Great.
- What's the latest news?

226
00:17:09.667 --> 00:17:10.833
Latest news?

227
00:17:11.167 --> 00:17:12.917
I've brought this Indian along.

228
00:17:13.542 --> 00:17:15.167
Let him stay here.

229
00:17:15.417 --> 00:17:17.833
We'll talk about
what to do with him tomorrow morning.

230
00:17:20.167 --> 00:17:21.625
Okay, sir.

231
00:17:22.625 --> 00:17:24.625
Go there. This is your workplace.

232
00:17:25.208 --> 00:17:26.208
Where?

233
00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:29.292
Karuvatta Sreekumar said that
we'd be working in a company.

234
00:17:29.417 --> 00:17:30.583
Go! Go with him!

235
00:17:31.125 --> 00:17:33.333
Come on! Go and sleep
somewhere over there.

236
00:17:34.333 --> 00:17:35.333
Is he leaving?

237
00:17:35.417 --> 00:17:37.083
I need to make a phone call.

238
00:17:37.167 --> 00:17:39.625
You can use the telephone tomorrow.
Now go!

239
00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:40.875
Bye-bye!

240
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.375
Bye! Inshallah!

241
00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.833
Oh, God! It's so cold!

242
00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:48.167
This year, it's even colder.

243
00:17:52.708 --> 00:17:53.792
Come on!

244
00:17:54.042 --> 00:17:55.750
It's time to sleep!

245
00:18:04.125 --> 00:18:05.333
Who is it?

246
00:18:10.042 --> 00:18:11.208
Who are you?

247
00:18:21.458 --> 00:18:22.458
What place is this?

248
00:18:23.458 --> 00:18:24.458
Oh!

249
00:18:25.333 --> 00:18:26.583
You're a Madrasi?

250
00:18:27.792 --> 00:18:29.250
Why have you come here?

251
00:18:31.417 --> 00:18:32.708
To work?

252
00:18:34.917 --> 00:18:36.000
Hindi…

253
00:18:37.667 --> 00:18:38.667
I'm a Malayali.

254
00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.000
Malayalam?

255
00:18:41.042 --> 00:18:42.958
Do you know
what kind of work is done here?

256
00:18:47.292 --> 00:18:48.958
Can I get some water to drink?

257
00:18:49.625 --> 00:18:50.625
Water.

258
00:18:50.875 --> 00:18:52.000
Water?

259
00:18:53.375 --> 00:18:54.375
Water is over there.

260
00:19:00.792 --> 00:19:03.292
What was he even thinking?

261
00:20:02.625 --> 00:20:03.625
Brother.

262
00:20:06.417 --> 00:20:08.042
Where do I sleep?

263
00:20:09.667 --> 00:20:10.667
What?

264
00:20:11.208 --> 00:20:12.625
What are you saying?

265
00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:15.375
Place to sleep?

266
00:20:16.167 --> 00:20:18.125
- Where do I...
- Sleep anywhere you want.

267
00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:23.500
Najeeb, that's enough!

268
00:22:23.708 --> 00:22:24.708
Let's get back.

269
00:22:25.875 --> 00:22:27.976
I need to scoop out six more
baskets of sand to meet the target.

270
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:30.500
The mason will give me an earful
if we wait to meet the target.

271
00:22:30.875 --> 00:22:32.795
We have molding work today.
Get back on the boat.

272
00:22:36.333 --> 00:22:37.708
What's with the new style?

273
00:22:38.125 --> 00:22:39.845
Have you switched
from <i>beedis </i>to cigarettes?

274
00:22:39.875 --> 00:22:41.375
Foreign cigarettes. Take one.

275
00:22:41.458 --> 00:22:42.768
My brother-in-law bought
them from the Middle East.

276
00:22:42.792 --> 00:22:43.792
No, thanks.

277
00:22:44.083 --> 00:22:45.083
Take one, man!

278
00:22:46.833 --> 00:22:48.917
Even without smoking,
I still can't stop coughing.

279
00:22:49.625 --> 00:22:51.458
You've had this cough for a while now.

280
00:22:52.125 --> 00:22:53.667
Go and see a doctor.

281
00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:55.870
If it turns out to be pneumonia,
you'll be in trouble!

282
00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:58.790
The doctor has asked me
to quit this job altogether.

283
00:22:59.042 --> 00:23:00.250
Is that even possible?

284
00:23:00.333 --> 00:23:01.458
Hey, Santhosh!

285
00:23:01.958 --> 00:23:05.039
Didn't your brother-in-law from Karuvatta
bring anything from the Middle East?

286
00:23:05.208 --> 00:23:06.375
He has brought two visas.

287
00:23:06.458 --> 00:23:07.708
Do you want to go abroad?

288
00:23:08.042 --> 00:23:10.583
I'm just waiting for
the visa from God.

289
00:23:10.708 --> 00:23:12.458
I needn't spend money on that, right?

290
00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.125
It's a free visa.

291
00:23:15.958 --> 00:23:18.458
Hey, Santhosh!
Is that thing about the visa true?

292
00:23:18.625 --> 00:23:20.000
Why? Do you want to go?

293
00:23:20.917 --> 00:23:22.750
It will cost a lot of money, right?

294
00:23:23.167 --> 00:23:24.792
It will cost at least 30,000 rupees.

295
00:23:25.292 --> 00:23:27.518
But you can earn it back with
just two months' salary, right?

296
00:23:27.542 --> 00:23:29.167
Thirty thousand rupees?

297
00:23:29.833 --> 00:23:31.292
I'll have to sell my house!

298
00:23:32.125 --> 00:23:34.750
Why do you have to sell it?
You can mortgage it, right?

299
00:23:35.125 --> 00:23:36.583
It's only a matter of two months.

300
00:23:46.458 --> 00:23:49.458
I've only studied up to the fifth grade.
What kind of job could I get?

301
00:23:49.625 --> 00:23:51.667
You're not going to work
as a bureaucrat there!

302
00:23:51.833 --> 00:23:54.601
Why do you need education to work
as a laborer? You have a passport, right?

303
00:23:54.625 --> 00:23:56.958
You arrange the money, man!
I'll get the visa ready.

304
00:24:17.125 --> 00:24:19.250
There he is.
The one in red.

305
00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:21.101
I told you
my brother-in-law would be here.

306
00:24:21.125 --> 00:24:23.917
As far as I can remember,
he has only missed this festival once.

307
00:24:24.042 --> 00:24:25.042
Last year.

308
00:24:25.208 --> 00:24:27.083
- During the Kuwait war.
- Okay.

309
00:24:27.167 --> 00:24:30.247
Otherwise, no matter where he is in
the world, he'll be here for the festival.

310
00:24:30.333 --> 00:24:32.417
Come on. Brother!

311
00:24:33.833 --> 00:24:34.833
Brother!

312
00:24:45.542 --> 00:24:46.625
Did you go to my house?

313
00:24:46.708 --> 00:24:48.583
I knew that you would be here.

314
00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:51.208
- This is Najeeb, the guy I told you about.
- Oh, yeah.

315
00:24:51.333 --> 00:24:52.458
I'm Sreekumar.

316
00:24:52.542 --> 00:24:54.750
People abroad know me
as Karuvatta Sreekumar.

317
00:24:54.958 --> 00:24:56.625
- Shall we step aside and talk?
- Sure.

318
00:24:57.792 --> 00:24:59.333
Hey! Why are you late?

319
00:24:59.458 --> 00:25:01.667
I cannot fly down like you, right?

320
00:25:01.750 --> 00:25:03.542
Yeah, right!
Don't pull my leg!

321
00:25:03.625 --> 00:25:04.625
Get going.

322
00:25:08.500 --> 00:25:10.708
I sold all my gold and other belongings

323
00:25:11.083 --> 00:25:12.583
to arrange this somehow.

324
00:25:13.417 --> 00:25:14.417
I know, man.

325
00:25:14.542 --> 00:25:16.542
All Middle East expats
cross the sea like this.

326
00:25:16.958 --> 00:25:20.208
Ask him what I had with me
when I got married to Kochammini.

327
00:25:20.708 --> 00:25:22.917
He was just a toddler running
around naked back then!

328
00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:24.542
You are too much, brother!

329
00:25:24.750 --> 00:25:26.708
I said that out of anxiety.

330
00:25:27.083 --> 00:25:28.833
If I get cheated…

331
00:25:29.708 --> 00:25:31.875
If you don't trust me,
you can have your money back.

332
00:25:32.125 --> 00:25:33.583
I agreed only because he forced me.

333
00:25:33.792 --> 00:25:36.875
There's a boy from Malappuram
who's joining this company as a helper.

334
00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:38.458
His father is in Dubai.

335
00:25:38.542 --> 00:25:40.268
If I plan to deceive them,
do you think they'll be fooled?

336
00:25:40.292 --> 00:25:42.667
No, brother!
That's not what I meant.

337
00:25:42.750 --> 00:25:43.750
- My...
- Brother…

338
00:25:43.917 --> 00:25:45.458
he has two brothers-in-law in Dubai.

339
00:25:45.625 --> 00:25:48.625
To be honest, he married his wife
with the intention of settling down there.

340
00:25:48.708 --> 00:25:49.583
Right?

341
00:25:49.667 --> 00:25:51.267
What's the point in mentioning that now?

342
00:25:51.333 --> 00:25:54.542
The anxiety of mortgaging my
house made me say that, brother.

343
00:25:54.875 --> 00:25:56.083
Please don't misunderstand me.

344
00:25:58.125 --> 00:25:59.250
You don't have to worry.

345
00:25:59.708 --> 00:26:01.143
- Does it contain the full amount?
- Yes.

346
00:26:01.167 --> 00:26:03.059
Pay the remaining 10,000 rupees
to the agent in Bombay.

347
00:26:03.083 --> 00:26:04.351
You'll only receive the visa then.

348
00:26:04.375 --> 00:26:06.458
- Got it? Shall I make a move then?
- Okay.

349
00:26:06.583 --> 00:26:09.000
Hey, I had told Kochammini
that you'd be coming home.

350
00:26:09.083 --> 00:26:10.750
Stop by there before you leave.

351
00:26:10.833 --> 00:26:12.083
Okay then! Carry on!

352
00:26:27.208 --> 00:26:29.750
We are taking the trouble of making
this unnecessarily, Sainu.

353
00:26:29.833 --> 00:26:32.583
While he enjoys buffalo meat
and biryani there,

354
00:26:32.667 --> 00:26:34.417
do you think he'll also eat your pickle?

355
00:26:35.000 --> 00:26:38.458
Mom, the wealthy Arabs
eat camel meat there.

356
00:26:38.792 --> 00:26:41.125
My brother, Nasser brought some
when he visited once.

357
00:26:42.833 --> 00:26:44.000
That reminds me!

358
00:26:44.292 --> 00:26:47.042
Get him the phone numbers
of Nasser and Hussain.

359
00:26:47.167 --> 00:26:49.333
They are his brothers-in-law after all.

360
00:26:49.417 --> 00:26:51.125
He can call them
in case of an emergency.

361
00:26:51.250 --> 00:26:52.417
Stop it, Mom!

362
00:26:52.542 --> 00:26:54.434
I begged and pleaded many times
with my dear brothers

363
00:26:54.458 --> 00:26:56.333
to arrange a visa for my husband.

364
00:26:56.875 --> 00:26:58.042
Did they even bother?

365
00:26:58.458 --> 00:26:59.708
Why do we need them now?

366
00:26:59.917 --> 00:27:01.684
I'm waiting for Najeeb's first
money order to reach us!

367
00:27:01.708 --> 00:27:04.958
I'm planning to purchase a copper vessel
from Mannattu and bring it home

368
00:27:05.208 --> 00:27:07.288
so that my sister-in-law
can cook some biryani in it.

369
00:27:07.708 --> 00:27:09.250
Mom, take this.

370
00:27:10.250 --> 00:27:13.125
Make a delicious mutton curry
with added coconut shavings.

371
00:27:13.208 --> 00:27:15.708
Don't get wet in the rain
and catch a fever before you leave.

372
00:27:16.958 --> 00:27:18.167
Or do you want biryani, Sainu?

373
00:27:19.042 --> 00:27:21.125
It's been a while since we had
Mom's biryani, right?

374
00:27:22.042 --> 00:27:24.208
I'd like to have Mom's
mutton biryani before I leave.

375
00:27:24.417 --> 00:27:25.417
What do you say?

376
00:27:25.708 --> 00:27:27.667
You should have bought
a goat's head too.

377
00:27:28.125 --> 00:27:29.667
I would have made
some soup for her.

378
00:27:29.875 --> 00:27:32.000
She needs to be eating properly
during this time.

379
00:27:32.292 --> 00:27:33.625
I have arranged that.

380
00:27:34.208 --> 00:27:35.333
You know Mammad, right?

381
00:27:37.250 --> 00:27:39.250
I'll finish eating this
before boarding the plane.

382
00:27:39.958 --> 00:27:43.417
I've asked Mammad to bring
a goat's head here every week

383
00:27:43.875 --> 00:27:44.917
until her delivery.

384
00:27:45.417 --> 00:27:47.583
After all, she's the wife
of a Middle East expat!

385
00:27:53.542 --> 00:27:55.042
This is full of chili powder!

386
00:27:55.542 --> 00:27:56.958
That's because you mocked me!

387
00:27:57.292 --> 00:27:59.500
Am I really that desperate
to drink soup here?

388
00:27:59.583 --> 00:28:02.292
The soup is not for you!
It's for my child!

389
00:28:02.458 --> 00:28:04.699
Mom, did you hear that?
She thought the soup was for her!

390
00:28:05.375 --> 00:28:06.708
Get out!
This is my tent!

391
00:28:08.750 --> 00:28:10.792
- Let me lie down here.
- Get out!

392
00:28:10.917 --> 00:28:12.684
- It's really cold outside...
- Bloody scoundrel!

393
00:28:12.708 --> 00:28:14.458
Idiot!
Don't you understand anything?

394
00:28:15.542 --> 00:28:17.542
- I'll sleep here.
- Listen, you scoundrel!

395
00:28:17.917 --> 00:28:20.458
If you repeat this,
I'll break your legs!

396
00:28:21.375 --> 00:28:22.375
I'll…

397
00:28:22.667 --> 00:28:27.125
Bloody moron!
How dare he enter my tent!

398
00:28:28.083 --> 00:28:29.667
Nuisance!

399
00:29:38.708 --> 00:29:42.500
The day you stop giving milk,

400
00:29:43.417 --> 00:29:44.833
you're dead meat.

401
00:29:48.583 --> 00:29:49.833
Hey, Madrasi!

402
00:29:51.083 --> 00:29:52.167
Come!

403
00:29:56.042 --> 00:29:57.042
Come here.

404
00:30:02.167 --> 00:30:03.333
I'm not from Madras.

405
00:30:06.292 --> 00:30:07.417
I'm from Kerala.

406
00:30:08.292 --> 00:30:09.292
Malayalam.

407
00:30:10.333 --> 00:30:11.333
Najeeb.

408
00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:13.667
What's your name, brother?

409
00:30:15.542 --> 00:30:18.375
Your… name?
What is your name?

410
00:30:19.708 --> 00:30:21.125
- My name?
- Yes.

411
00:30:21.458 --> 00:30:22.500
I don't remember.

412
00:30:25.917 --> 00:30:28.583
Take this milk to him inside.

413
00:30:30.708 --> 00:30:31.708
Hindi…

414
00:30:32.583 --> 00:30:33.583
No?

415
00:30:33.958 --> 00:30:35.458
I don't understand Hindi.

416
00:30:35.542 --> 00:30:38.500
Take… this milk… inside.

417
00:30:46.583 --> 00:30:47.708
You scoundrel!

418
00:30:48.042 --> 00:30:50.083
Who asked you to drink it?

419
00:30:50.292 --> 00:30:52.012
- Didn't you ask me to drink it?
- Get lost!

420
00:30:52.417 --> 00:30:53.417
Fool!

421
00:30:57.875 --> 00:30:59.042
How do I make you understand?

422
00:30:59.208 --> 00:31:00.583
This is not for you.

423
00:31:01.375 --> 00:31:03.875
This is for the Kafeel.

424
00:31:04.542 --> 00:31:06.417
The Arab! Over there!

425
00:31:06.708 --> 00:31:07.792
Give it to him.

426
00:31:08.375 --> 00:31:09.375
Go!

427
00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.708
Of all people, the Kafeel
had to bring this Madrasi!

428
00:31:16.458 --> 00:31:17.750
Useless!

429
00:31:27.250 --> 00:31:28.542
Praise be to Allah!

430
00:31:32.333 --> 00:31:34.583
Allah, protect me from all evil.

431
00:31:37.292 --> 00:31:38.292
What is with you?

432
00:31:38.875 --> 00:31:40.208
What are you doing over there?

433
00:31:41.458 --> 00:31:43.250
Come on in!
Bring it here!

434
00:31:51.500 --> 00:31:53.667
- Peace be upon you.
- Peace be upon you as well.

435
00:31:54.208 --> 00:31:55.292
Do you know Arabic?

436
00:32:04.875 --> 00:32:05.875
He knows Hindi.

437
00:32:05.958 --> 00:32:08.167
Talk to him and learn
what has to be done here. Go.

438
00:32:10.875 --> 00:32:12.917
Do you understand what
I'm saying? Do you?

439
00:32:14.375 --> 00:32:15.667
I don't understand Arabic.

440
00:32:15.917 --> 00:32:18.208
Go to him and learn how
to do the job. Quick!

441
00:32:19.708 --> 00:32:21.000
What were you doing before this?

442
00:32:21.250 --> 00:32:22.250
Malayalam.

443
00:32:22.958 --> 00:32:23.958
Kerala.

444
00:32:24.750 --> 00:32:25.625
India…

445
00:32:25.708 --> 00:32:27.518
I don't understand the Hindi language
you're blabbering.

446
00:32:27.542 --> 00:32:29.042
Listen, don't give me a headache.

447
00:32:29.167 --> 00:32:31.767
Watch that guy who speaks Hindi,
learn from him, and do your work.

448
00:32:31.875 --> 00:32:32.875
- Go!
- Sir!

449
00:32:32.958 --> 00:32:34.542
For God's sake, please save me.

450
00:32:34.625 --> 00:32:36.000
I came here to work for a company.

451
00:32:36.708 --> 00:32:38.667
For God's sake, please save me.
I beg you!

452
00:32:38.750 --> 00:32:41.042
Go away! What is this?
May you be damned!

453
00:32:41.250 --> 00:32:43.708
I sold everything I had to pay for…

454
00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:45.000
Damn you!

455
00:32:45.167 --> 00:32:47.625
Sir, how do I even…

456
00:32:48.250 --> 00:32:50.125
Let me leave.
I shall go back.

457
00:32:50.208 --> 00:32:52.750
- I shall go back!
- Go! Go away!

458
00:32:54.625 --> 00:32:56.625
Hey, Hindi! Come here.
Teach him how to do the job!

459
00:32:59.250 --> 00:33:00.500
There's no point…

460
00:33:01.417 --> 00:33:02.792
in crying.

461
00:33:20.458 --> 00:33:21.458
Go!

462
00:33:22.208 --> 00:33:23.208
Go away!

463
00:33:23.667 --> 00:33:24.667
Go!

464
00:33:38.542 --> 00:33:39.583
Oh, Allah!

465
00:33:44.708 --> 00:33:45.833
Peace be upon you.

466
00:33:48.333 --> 00:33:49.458
I paid money...

467
00:33:49.750 --> 00:33:52.750
They took money from me for the visa,
promising a job in a company,

468
00:33:53.667 --> 00:33:55.417
along with an AC room to stay

469
00:33:55.625 --> 00:33:56.667
and good food.

470
00:33:56.792 --> 00:33:57.792
He cheated me!

471
00:33:57.833 --> 00:33:58.917
Karuvatta Sreekumar…

472
00:33:59.000 --> 00:33:59.875
Kafeel!

473
00:33:59.958 --> 00:34:00.833
Peace be upon you.

474
00:34:00.917 --> 00:34:02.226
- Peace be upon you as well.
- How are you doing?

475
00:34:02.250 --> 00:34:04.268
- I hope you are doing good.
- I need to make a phone call.

476
00:34:04.292 --> 00:34:05.167
- All good.
- Sir…

477
00:34:05.250 --> 00:34:07.333
Go and keep that sack inside.
Don't trouble me.

478
00:34:07.458 --> 00:34:09.292
I need to call my family.

479
00:34:09.833 --> 00:34:12.375
Oh, God!
Don't you understand?

480
00:34:12.542 --> 00:34:15.458
Take that sack inside.
Don't drive me crazy!

481
00:34:21.917 --> 00:34:23.309
He will learn everything
in due course.

482
00:34:23.333 --> 00:34:25.393
Seems quite difficult.
He doesn't understand anything.

483
00:34:25.417 --> 00:34:27.750
- He will understand, just like the guy…
- Oh, God!

484
00:34:27.917 --> 00:34:29.708
How do I make them understand?

485
00:34:35.583 --> 00:34:36.583
Get up!

486
00:34:37.583 --> 00:34:39.000
Take this.

487
00:34:39.125 --> 00:34:40.125
What is this for?

488
00:34:41.083 --> 00:34:43.292
I will leave.
Let me go back.

489
00:34:43.542 --> 00:34:46.167
- Please let me...
- Listen to me. Wear it!

490
00:34:46.833 --> 00:34:49.125
- I don't...
- You better listen to him!

491
00:34:49.375 --> 00:34:50.542
Go and wear it!

492
00:34:50.750 --> 00:34:52.833
I sold everything I had to come here.

493
00:34:52.917 --> 00:34:55.292
I'm sure he won't understand
anything. Such a nuisance!

494
00:34:55.542 --> 00:34:57.042
Please hear me out, sir.

495
00:34:57.333 --> 00:34:59.792
I arranged the money to come here
by mortgaging my house.

496
00:35:00.250 --> 00:35:02.500
He thinks that we can
understand his language!

497
00:35:02.583 --> 00:35:03.583
Unbelievable.

498
00:35:04.208 --> 00:35:05.208
I…

499
00:35:12.625 --> 00:35:16.833
I paid 20,000 rupees to this person
who said he would give it to the Kafeel.

500
00:35:17.375 --> 00:35:18.750
Karuvatta Sreekumar.

501
00:35:21.208 --> 00:35:24.417
Even the agent in Bombay
took 10,000 rupees from me.

502
00:35:27.542 --> 00:35:28.792
- Papers?
- Yes.

503
00:35:29.500 --> 00:35:30.792
Hey! What are you doing?

504
00:35:31.208 --> 00:35:32.208
Don't tear it!

505
00:35:32.500 --> 00:35:34.708
- That's mine…
- How dare you!

506
00:35:38.833 --> 00:35:41.194
Keep an eye on him so he
doesn't cause trouble for us later.

507
00:35:41.958 --> 00:35:43.125
Don't bother about that.

508
00:35:43.458 --> 00:35:45.138
He's new here.
He'll learn everything soon.

509
00:35:45.750 --> 00:35:46.792
Come on.

510
00:36:06.792 --> 00:36:08.333
Let us begin,
in the name of Allah.

511
00:36:20.292 --> 00:36:21.292
Come here!

512
00:36:22.458 --> 00:36:23.458
Come here, man!

513
00:36:26.542 --> 00:36:27.625
I asked you to come!

514
00:36:28.292 --> 00:36:29.292
Come!

515
00:36:38.917 --> 00:36:40.500
Friend, come here!

516
00:36:42.708 --> 00:36:43.958
Come. Have some bread.

517
00:36:45.208 --> 00:36:46.833
Bread! Bread!
This is bread!

518
00:37:01.917 --> 00:37:02.917
Look at him!

519
00:37:03.417 --> 00:37:06.542
There's a saying
that bread can revive a person!

520
00:37:07.708 --> 00:37:08.917
You are right, sir.

521
00:37:09.625 --> 00:37:11.250
Come on! Come!

522
00:37:17.708 --> 00:37:19.208
Sit down! Sit!

523
00:37:27.917 --> 00:37:28.917
Take it.

524
00:37:29.875 --> 00:37:30.875
Take it.

525
00:37:40.917 --> 00:37:42.517
Didn't I tell you that
he must be hungry?

526
00:37:42.750 --> 00:37:44.270
That's why he was so
angry and finicky.

527
00:37:44.417 --> 00:37:45.500
That's right.

528
00:37:46.417 --> 00:37:47.417
Here you go!

529
00:37:47.708 --> 00:37:49.000
Take one more piece.

530
00:37:50.042 --> 00:37:51.042
Take it.

531
00:37:57.417 --> 00:37:59.458
Be quick in learning
how to do the job, okay?

532
00:37:59.792 --> 00:38:00.792
You heard me?

533
00:38:04.708 --> 00:38:06.083
Drink some water.

534
00:38:07.667 --> 00:38:08.667
Have it.

535
00:38:08.750 --> 00:38:09.750
Drink it.

536
00:38:10.208 --> 00:38:11.250
Drink it.

537
00:38:22.708 --> 00:38:23.750
It's okay. Look.

538
00:38:25.375 --> 00:38:26.375
Do this.

539
00:38:32.333 --> 00:38:33.333
Do it.

540
00:38:35.958 --> 00:38:37.000
Dip it like this…

541
00:38:39.083 --> 00:38:40.125
and eat it like this.

542
00:39:29.708 --> 00:39:30.708
Brother!

543
00:39:34.167 --> 00:39:35.167
Brother!

544
00:39:45.583 --> 00:39:48.292
Why are you frightening my goats?

545
00:39:50.208 --> 00:39:51.208
Oh, no!

546
00:39:51.625 --> 00:39:52.667
Where…

547
00:39:54.250 --> 00:39:55.958
Road… main road…

548
00:39:56.292 --> 00:39:57.292
Where is it?

549
00:39:57.542 --> 00:39:58.667
Road?

550
00:39:58.750 --> 00:39:59.792
Yes.

551
00:40:01.375 --> 00:40:02.542
Far away!

552
00:40:03.583 --> 00:40:05.000
Far, far away!

553
00:40:06.417 --> 00:40:09.750
Who knows how far!

554
00:40:40.250 --> 00:40:42.451
I feel like I'm trapped
in the middle of the sea, Sainu.

555
00:40:45.167 --> 00:40:46.917
How do I inform you about this?

556
00:41:21.833 --> 00:41:24.792
TO MY DEAR SAINU…

557
00:41:26.667 --> 00:41:28.167
<i>Look at the sky.</i>

558
00:41:28.375 --> 00:41:31.208
<i>Can't you see the moon
resembling a sliver of coconut?</i>

559
00:41:52.667 --> 00:41:55.667
Even if you can't call me,
just think of me when you see the moon…

560
00:41:57.292 --> 00:41:58.750
wherever you are on this earth.

561
00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:07.875
God has answered my prayers.

562
00:42:10.500 --> 00:42:12.750
It must be the good fortune
of our child.

563
00:42:16.250 --> 00:42:17.542
I'm not asking for much.

564
00:42:18.292 --> 00:42:20.833
We need a room of our own,

565
00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:22.875
a place to sit and talk like this.

566
00:42:23.625 --> 00:42:27.167
Can we sneak into someone else's boat
like this once we have a child?

567
00:42:28.667 --> 00:42:31.208
We need to fix the leaks in our kitchen.

568
00:42:32.417 --> 00:42:33.542
And…

569
00:42:34.875 --> 00:42:37.375
we should send our son
to a good school.

570
00:42:38.083 --> 00:42:39.333
That's all I need.

571
00:42:40.167 --> 00:42:42.047
Have you decided that
we're going to have a son?

572
00:42:42.292 --> 00:42:43.458
Don't you want a daughter?

573
00:42:43.917 --> 00:42:45.042
I want a daughter as well.

574
00:42:45.542 --> 00:42:47.262
Shouldn't we educate her
and raise her well?

575
00:42:47.708 --> 00:42:48.917
Shouldn't we get her married?

576
00:42:49.708 --> 00:42:51.417
You'll be an old man by then!

577
00:42:51.875 --> 00:42:53.542
At most four or five years.

578
00:42:53.792 --> 00:42:55.250
Come back after that.

579
00:42:55.750 --> 00:42:56.958
That's more than enough.

580
00:42:58.083 --> 00:42:59.458
- Is it?
- Yes.

581
00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:02.500
Alright then.

582
00:43:03.208 --> 00:43:06.292
Now, let me give my baby a kiss.

583
00:43:11.667 --> 00:43:12.750
Nabeel!

584
00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:14.042
Nabeel?

585
00:43:14.458 --> 00:43:15.917
What if it's a girl?

586
00:43:17.792 --> 00:43:18.917
Safiya.

587
00:43:20.792 --> 00:43:21.792
Nabeel.

588
00:43:22.292 --> 00:43:23.333
Safiya.

589
00:43:32.375 --> 00:43:34.208
I think the train is about to arrive.

590
00:43:37.167 --> 00:43:38.167
Son!

591
00:43:42.333 --> 00:43:45.042
God will be with you.
I will pray for you.

592
00:43:49.292 --> 00:43:52.000
I… will inform the local phone booth.

593
00:43:52.792 --> 00:43:54.000
You can wait there.

594
00:43:54.667 --> 00:43:55.667
Okay?

595
00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:00.792
Shall I go?

596
00:44:01.833 --> 00:44:04.500
Mom… take care of Sainu.

597
00:44:14.542 --> 00:44:15.708
Brother, please move.

598
00:44:50.583 --> 00:44:51.583
This is the one.

599
00:44:51.667 --> 00:44:53.018
- What's your seat number?
- Thirty-nine.

600
00:44:53.042 --> 00:44:54.375
Easy. Careful.

601
00:44:56.542 --> 00:44:57.542
Okay.

602
00:44:57.583 --> 00:44:58.667
I…

603
00:45:02.250 --> 00:45:03.708
You're leaving with a small bag.

604
00:45:03.792 --> 00:45:06.000
But make sure to bring big suitcases
when you come back!

605
00:45:06.083 --> 00:45:07.083
Sure.

606
00:45:07.292 --> 00:45:08.292
It's over here.

607
00:45:08.667 --> 00:45:10.833
Brother, it's okay even if you
don't bring anything.

608
00:45:11.125 --> 00:45:12.708
But just don't forget about the visas.

609
00:45:12.833 --> 00:45:13.708
Okay.

610
00:45:13.792 --> 00:45:14.893
Come on.
The train will leave now.

611
00:45:14.917 --> 00:45:16.143
- Shall we leave, brother?
- Yes.

612
00:45:16.167 --> 00:45:17.333
Happy journey, Najeeb!

613
00:45:17.667 --> 00:45:19.542
He's leaving his house
for the first time.

614
00:45:19.833 --> 00:45:21.458
I feel relieved because
you are with him.

615
00:45:21.667 --> 00:45:23.726
That's why we came here from
Malappuram, to board the train.

616
00:45:23.750 --> 00:45:25.042
- Take care of him.
- Okay.

617
00:45:25.292 --> 00:45:27.542
Mom, don't be so anxious.

618
00:45:27.750 --> 00:45:28.750
- Okay?
- Najeeb.

619
00:45:28.875 --> 00:45:30.458
Call me as soon as you
arrive in Bombay.

620
00:45:31.292 --> 00:45:32.333
I will call you.

621
00:45:33.333 --> 00:45:34.814
Don't get drenched and catch a fever.

622
00:45:36.292 --> 00:45:37.292
Mom…

623
00:45:37.542 --> 00:45:39.333
take her to the doctor, okay?

624
00:46:51.542 --> 00:46:52.583
You bloody dog!

625
00:46:52.750 --> 00:46:54.417
We pay money to buy this water!

626
00:46:54.583 --> 00:46:56.667
The water is intended for use
in our work here.

627
00:46:56.792 --> 00:46:58.726
- I was just...
- Do you know the value of water here?

628
00:46:58.750 --> 00:47:00.000
I was taking a dump!

629
00:47:00.917 --> 00:47:03.667
If you touch it again,
I'll chop off your hands!

630
00:47:04.542 --> 00:47:07.393
- If you take the water away, how will I...
- I pay money for it and he's wasting it!

631
00:47:07.417 --> 00:47:08.542
Water!

632
00:47:08.917 --> 00:47:10.708
He pays good money to buy water!

633
00:47:14.167 --> 00:47:15.708
Without water, how do I…

634
00:47:16.292 --> 00:47:17.500
This is so bothersome!

635
00:47:17.667 --> 00:47:19.167
Not water!

636
00:47:21.708 --> 00:47:22.792
Use sand!

637
00:47:29.458 --> 00:47:30.667
Damn it!

638
00:47:41.167 --> 00:47:42.167
Brother!

639
00:47:42.458 --> 00:47:43.750
Can you take me with you?

640
00:47:43.833 --> 00:47:44.833
What?

641
00:47:44.958 --> 00:47:48.208
When you head back,
can I ride with you in your vehicle?

642
00:47:48.375 --> 00:47:50.518
What are you saying, brother?
I don't understand anything.

643
00:47:50.542 --> 00:47:51.958
To the road. In your vehicle.

644
00:47:52.083 --> 00:47:53.625
Can you take me with you?

645
00:47:53.708 --> 00:47:55.250
What did this rascal tell you?

646
00:47:56.333 --> 00:47:58.333
- I don't know.
- You don't know?

647
00:47:59.000 --> 00:48:00.208
Come here.
Where are you going?

648
00:48:00.708 --> 00:48:01.708
Come here.

649
00:48:02.667 --> 00:48:03.708
I know what he said.

650
00:48:04.333 --> 00:48:07.333
Wasn't he asking you
to help him escape?

651
00:48:07.417 --> 00:48:08.417
No.

652
00:48:11.500 --> 00:48:12.625
What were you telling him?

653
00:48:13.542 --> 00:48:14.542
I didn't say anything.

654
00:48:15.458 --> 00:48:17.042
I overheard you talking to him!

655
00:48:17.458 --> 00:48:19.667
What were you blabbering to him?

656
00:48:20.250 --> 00:48:21.417
I didn't tell him anything.

657
00:48:22.417 --> 00:48:25.292
- Didn't you hear me?
- Why are you hitting me?

658
00:48:25.417 --> 00:48:27.583
- What did you…
- I didn't say anything!

659
00:48:27.667 --> 00:48:28.667
Let me go!

660
00:48:28.750 --> 00:48:30.000
Let me go back!

661
00:48:30.292 --> 00:48:31.458
I will go back!

662
00:48:33.958 --> 00:48:35.083
You're fighting back?

663
00:48:36.250 --> 00:48:38.292
Bloody scoundrel!
I'll teach you a lesson!

664
00:48:39.125 --> 00:48:40.292
I'll show you!

665
00:48:45.417 --> 00:48:46.958
What did he tell you?

666
00:48:47.167 --> 00:48:49.542
I don't know.
The Kafeel was saying something.

667
00:48:49.667 --> 00:48:52.042
Don't mess with him.

668
00:48:52.708 --> 00:48:54.667
He can do anything.

669
00:49:00.083 --> 00:49:01.375
You bloody scoundrel!

670
00:49:01.958 --> 00:49:03.167
Bloody devil!

671
00:49:03.750 --> 00:49:05.393
Do you think you can
fight back against me?

672
00:49:05.417 --> 00:49:07.250
Sure! I'll kill you, you bloody dog!

673
00:49:07.333 --> 00:49:08.875
Boss, he didn't
tell me anything.

674
00:49:09.083 --> 00:49:10.167
You shut up!

675
00:49:10.542 --> 00:49:12.102
You don't need to get involved in this!

676
00:49:12.167 --> 00:49:14.542
Why are you shouting at him?
He didn't tell me anything.

677
00:49:14.875 --> 00:49:16.333
I didn't tell him anything.

678
00:49:16.958 --> 00:49:18.167
You're grabbing my gun?

679
00:49:18.750 --> 00:49:22.750
I'll pull the trigger
and blow your head off!

680
00:49:27.750 --> 00:49:29.208
How dare you fight me, you dog?

681
00:49:29.792 --> 00:49:31.750
I'll kill you and bury you
in this desert.

682
00:49:35.167 --> 00:49:36.167
Understood?

683
00:49:40.042 --> 00:49:41.125
What are you staring at?

684
00:49:41.792 --> 00:49:43.232
Can't you see the water overflowing?

685
00:49:43.292 --> 00:49:44.208
Come on!

686
00:49:44.292 --> 00:49:45.958
Idiots! You are all stupid!

687
00:51:12.625 --> 00:51:13.625
Hey, girl!

688
00:51:14.375 --> 00:51:15.893
Aren't you ashamed to bathe like this?

689
00:51:15.917 --> 00:51:16.833
What's there to be ashamed of?

690
00:51:16.917 --> 00:51:18.708
I'm bathing inside the bathroom.

691
00:51:19.625 --> 00:51:22.265
We have such a beautiful river here.
You should be diving in there!

692
00:51:22.333 --> 00:51:24.000
Hey, Najeeb! What are you doing?

693
00:51:24.125 --> 00:51:25.125
Someone might see!

694
00:51:25.792 --> 00:51:27.184
I'm going to take you to the river today.

695
00:51:27.208 --> 00:51:28.292
Hey, Najeeb!

696
00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:31.000
Hey!

697
00:51:31.042 --> 00:51:32.667
No! Najeeb, I feel shy!

698
00:51:33.667 --> 00:51:36.083
- Let go of me, Najeeb!
- Don't tremble!

699
00:51:36.708 --> 00:51:39.667
- Mom, please ask him to leave me!
- What are you doing?

700
00:51:39.792 --> 00:51:41.208
Where are you taking her?

701
00:51:41.458 --> 00:51:44.042
Didn't you mention that
Dad carried you to the market?

702
00:51:44.167 --> 00:51:46.583
But I was only 12 years old back then!

703
00:51:46.667 --> 00:51:47.542
Mom!

704
00:51:47.667 --> 00:51:50.042
Well, she's ten years older than that.
It's fine.

705
00:51:50.167 --> 00:51:51.750
Let go of me! I'm scared!

706
00:51:52.083 --> 00:51:54.208
Hey, Najeeb!
Hasn't it been nearly a year?

707
00:51:54.292 --> 00:51:56.125
Is there no end to your craving even now?

708
00:51:56.208 --> 00:51:59.000
Brother, my craving won't be satisfied
until her shyness disappears.

709
00:51:59.167 --> 00:52:00.667
Hey! What are you saying?

710
00:52:00.750 --> 00:52:03.391
I'm going to make you overcome
your fear of getting into the river.

711
00:52:39.208 --> 00:52:40.208
Are you scared?

712
00:52:45.000 --> 00:52:46.208
I'm scared!

713
00:52:53.208 --> 00:52:57.917
<i>Within these eyes
That yearn for you</i>

714
00:52:59.042 --> 00:53:02.750
<i>Desire overflows like a lagoon's blue</i>

715
00:53:02.833 --> 00:53:06.417
<i>Together we sit, yet I crave you more</i>

716
00:53:06.667 --> 00:53:10.333
<i>And I swim in the depths
Embracing your core</i>

717
00:53:10.417 --> 00:53:14.125
<i>My mind, like white sand
Gleams so fine</i>

718
00:53:14.333 --> 00:53:19.000
<i>Lit by the sunshine of your smile divine</i>

719
00:53:19.167 --> 00:53:22.750
<i>On a moonlit bed
A thousand flowers fallen</i>

720
00:53:22.833 --> 00:53:25.167
<i>A sight so tender</i>

721
00:53:25.250 --> 00:53:30.375
<i>My bangles break
In your embrace, I surrender</i>

722
00:53:30.458 --> 00:53:34.083
<i>Within these eyes
That yearn for you</i>

723
00:53:34.292 --> 00:53:37.958
<i>Desire overflows like a lagoon's blue</i>

724
00:53:38.042 --> 00:53:41.667
<i>Together we sit, yet I crave you more</i>

725
00:53:41.833 --> 00:53:45.792
<i>And I swim in the depths
Embracing your core</i>

726
00:53:45.875 --> 00:53:49.625
<i>The yearning of our first night
Full of delight</i>

727
00:53:49.750 --> 00:53:53.417
<i>Still lingers in my thoughts
Day and night</i>

728
00:53:53.542 --> 00:53:57.333
<i>It poured like rain
In monsoon season</i>

729
00:53:57.417 --> 00:54:01.083
<i>Carrying me like a stream
With no reason</i>

730
00:54:01.167 --> 00:54:07.958
<i>Beloved, I was lost in the blue
My search was always, only for you</i>

731
00:54:08.625 --> 00:54:11.833
<i>Flow towards me as a cool breeze
Tender and slight</i>

732
00:54:12.292 --> 00:54:19.042
<i>To touch and wrap my tender form
In your wings, take flight</i>

733
00:54:19.917 --> 00:54:25.042
<i>Will we grow weary of love's endless swell
Within the river's swirling spell?</i>

734
00:54:25.167 --> 00:54:30.750
<i>To me, you're bound, night and day
Unable to separate, come what may</i>

735
00:54:31.167 --> 00:54:34.917
<i>Amidst petals in bloom
So lovely to view</i>

736
00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:39.167
<i>Within me remains
What I can't bestow on you</i>

737
00:55:32.417 --> 00:55:36.375
<i>O dreams that flower</i>

738
00:55:36.708 --> 00:55:40.000
<i>Amidst heaven's jasmine cart</i>

739
00:55:40.167 --> 00:55:44.042
<i>Do you see the love</i>

740
00:55:44.292 --> 00:55:47.958
<i>The bride holds in her heart?</i>

741
00:55:48.167 --> 00:55:51.583
<i>Can you glimpse her love
Pure and apart?</i>

742
00:55:51.667 --> 00:55:55.417
<i>The trees that grew all around</i>

743
00:55:55.708 --> 00:55:59.125
<i>Are now in bloom, O girl!</i>

744
00:55:59.292 --> 00:56:03.333
<i>Are pearls shining in the eyes</i>

745
00:56:03.458 --> 00:56:07.167
<i>Where a thousand stories unfurl?</i>

746
00:56:07.250 --> 00:56:10.667
<i>Are pearls gleaming in this lovely swirl?</i>

747
00:56:11.042 --> 00:56:14.792
<i>Are pearls gleaming in this lovely swirl?</i>

748
00:56:14.875 --> 00:56:17.833
<i>Are pearls gleaming in this lovely swirl?</i>

749
00:56:18.083 --> 00:56:21.750
<i>Like fish in water
Let's embrace and sway</i>

750
00:56:21.833 --> 00:56:25.417
<i>Through this silver stream
All night and day</i>

751
00:56:25.708 --> 00:56:29.333
<i>In all the songs I sing about you</i>

752
00:56:29.500 --> 00:56:33.042
<i>Droplets of love shine and drip anew</i>

753
00:56:33.292 --> 00:56:37.042
<i>Your body, a river of gold so true</i>

754
00:56:37.125 --> 00:56:41.708
<i>Touched by my dreams
As morning rays do</i>

755
00:56:41.917 --> 00:56:47.958
<i>As a moonlight vine
Wrapping your skin tight</i>

756
00:56:48.083 --> 00:56:52.583
<i>Bringing endless joy
Day and night</i>

757
00:56:52.667 --> 00:56:59.583
<i>Amidst the swaying mangrove flowers</i>

758
00:57:00.167 --> 00:57:03.875
<i>Your scent rushes</i>

759
00:57:04.000 --> 00:57:07.667
<i>Like blooming jasmines for hours</i>

760
00:57:07.792 --> 00:57:14.333
<i>O my beloved
Into the moonlight's depths I dove</i>

761
00:57:14.417 --> 00:57:17.917
<i>Within these eyes
That yearn for you</i>

762
00:57:18.000 --> 00:57:21.500
<i>Desire overflows like a lagoon's blue</i>

763
00:57:21.917 --> 00:57:25.417
<i>Together we sit, yet I crave you more</i>

764
00:57:25.542 --> 00:57:30.375
<i>And I swim in the depths
Embracing your core</i>

765
00:58:21.167 --> 00:58:22.167
Sainu…

766
00:58:30.917 --> 00:58:31.917
Sainu…

767
00:58:39.292 --> 00:58:41.250
Sainu!

768
00:58:46.792 --> 00:58:50.750
Even after eating so much, you're still…

769
00:58:51.417 --> 00:58:53.625
making these noises.

770
00:58:55.042 --> 00:58:56.125
I think…

771
00:58:57.583 --> 00:59:03.500
I'll die trying to feed you guys.

772
00:59:06.167 --> 00:59:07.167
Brother…

773
00:59:10.375 --> 00:59:11.667
Where have you been?

774
00:59:13.500 --> 00:59:14.625
How long has it been…

775
00:59:16.500 --> 00:59:18.875
How long has it been
since you came here?

776
00:59:23.458 --> 00:59:28.958
No one inside can go outside.

777
00:59:32.333 --> 00:59:34.833
It's a very famous song!

778
00:59:35.250 --> 00:59:40.625
<i>No one inside can go outside</i>

779
00:59:42.375 --> 00:59:47.458
<i>No one outside can come inside</i>

780
01:00:00.833 --> 01:00:02.250
Hey, Hindi!
Get up!

781
01:00:05.917 --> 01:00:06.917
Come on!

782
01:00:09.208 --> 01:00:10.667
It's already late! Come on!

783
01:00:26.667 --> 01:00:28.417
Milk the goats and bring me the milk.

784
01:00:29.750 --> 01:00:31.458
Milk the goats and bring me the milk!

785
01:00:38.042 --> 01:00:40.000
Come on!
Milk the goats and bring me the milk.

786
01:00:41.625 --> 01:00:43.417
Come and milk the goats!
Hurry up!

787
01:00:46.000 --> 01:00:47.250
Come on!

788
01:00:47.417 --> 01:00:50.333
Quick! How can you still be sleeping
when the sun is already up?

789
01:00:50.958 --> 01:00:52.083
Oh, God!

790
01:00:52.583 --> 01:00:53.667
What is he saying?

791
01:00:54.250 --> 01:00:55.792
Come here and milk the goats.

792
01:00:56.917 --> 01:00:57.917
I…

793
01:00:58.708 --> 01:01:00.458
I don't know how to milk the goats.

794
01:01:01.208 --> 01:01:03.542
Milk them like this. Understood?

795
01:01:05.583 --> 01:01:06.667
I…

796
01:01:07.708 --> 01:01:09.042
How do I tell him that I don't…

797
01:01:09.625 --> 01:01:10.875
Come on.
Come quickly.

798
01:01:11.167 --> 01:01:13.875
I don't know… how to milk them.

799
01:01:14.333 --> 01:01:17.208
- I don't know…
- Come on. Come quickly.

800
01:01:33.958 --> 01:01:35.208
You idiot!

801
01:01:35.375 --> 01:01:37.576
Don't try to milk it from the back.
You will get kicked!

802
01:01:37.792 --> 01:01:40.000
Approach from the front
and gently befriend it.

803
01:01:41.417 --> 01:01:43.458
I don't know how to do this job.

804
01:01:44.500 --> 01:01:45.792
Where's that Hindi guy?

805
01:01:46.333 --> 01:01:47.333
Listen.

806
01:01:47.750 --> 01:01:50.708
Hold its legs, and keep them
in between your legs…

807
01:01:51.417 --> 01:01:52.583
and then stroke it slowly.

808
01:01:53.208 --> 01:01:54.375
Then try holding it.

809
01:01:55.042 --> 01:01:57.208
And then, try milking it slowly.

810
01:01:57.500 --> 01:01:58.542
Understood?

811
01:01:59.542 --> 01:02:00.542
The Hindi guy?

812
01:02:01.583 --> 01:02:02.958
Isn't this his job?

813
01:02:03.958 --> 01:02:05.042
What…

814
01:02:05.750 --> 01:02:06.917
What happened to him?

815
01:02:07.458 --> 01:02:09.542
Stop blabbering and listen to me.

816
01:02:09.792 --> 01:02:12.667
You also have other tasks to complete.
Don't cause trouble for me!

817
01:02:12.958 --> 01:02:15.250
There are other jobs to do after this.
Go on!

818
01:02:16.667 --> 01:02:17.750
Milk the goats.

819
01:02:26.208 --> 01:02:28.333
There are things to do!
Hurry up!

820
01:02:28.792 --> 01:02:32.208
This guy is the limit!
When is he going to learn all this?

821
01:02:39.958 --> 01:02:40.958
Please…

822
01:02:42.083 --> 01:02:43.417
please don't get me beaten up.

823
01:02:44.583 --> 01:02:45.583
I…

824
01:02:46.583 --> 01:02:47.958
I don't know how to do this job.

825
01:03:12.417 --> 01:03:13.417
Go!

826
01:03:14.167 --> 01:03:15.167
Go!

827
01:03:21.083 --> 01:03:22.083
Go!

828
01:03:22.625 --> 01:03:23.625
Go!

829
01:03:24.250 --> 01:03:25.250
Go!

830
01:03:29.500 --> 01:03:30.500
Hey!

831
01:03:43.167 --> 01:03:44.792
What are you doing, you idiot?

832
01:04:09.708 --> 01:04:11.167
Are you fighting with the goats?

833
01:04:19.500 --> 01:04:20.542
Get up!

834
01:04:36.042 --> 01:04:37.917
Get up! Are you crazy?

835
01:04:38.208 --> 01:04:40.009
Be thankful to your Gods
that you're not dead.

836
01:04:54.958 --> 01:04:55.958
That's enough!

837
01:04:56.625 --> 01:04:58.375
Go and take the goats back.

838
01:04:58.833 --> 01:05:01.167
I won't give you another drop of water.

839
01:05:01.333 --> 01:05:03.125
Get up! Take this.
Get up!

840
01:05:03.667 --> 01:05:05.792
Come on! Get up!

841
01:05:15.417 --> 01:05:16.417
Get up!

842
01:05:17.042 --> 01:05:18.250
Get up!
Go on, bring the goats.

843
01:05:25.083 --> 01:05:27.583
I'm hurt.
I need to go to the hospital.

844
01:05:29.417 --> 01:05:30.750
I need to go to the hospital.

845
01:05:30.917 --> 01:05:34.250
Stop blabbering
and take the goats back. Go!

846
01:05:34.500 --> 01:05:36.292
I need to go to the hospital.

847
01:05:36.583 --> 01:05:38.417
I asked you to take them back!

848
01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:41.250
Hurry up!

849
01:05:41.833 --> 01:05:43.292
This guy is so bothersome!

850
01:05:52.667 --> 01:05:54.250
I can't do this.

851
01:05:56.458 --> 01:05:57.625
Allah!

852
01:06:01.958 --> 01:06:03.292
Allah!

853
01:07:38.000 --> 01:07:41.083
This is such a terrible situation.
Everyone has started buying machines.

854
01:07:41.583 --> 01:07:43.667
But you're still the same.

855
01:07:44.583 --> 01:07:46.464
You won't finish cutting this
even in one month.

856
01:07:46.958 --> 01:07:48.500
This is easier than using a machine.

857
01:07:48.875 --> 01:07:50.356
We've practiced this for a while now.

858
01:07:50.875 --> 01:07:52.292
You are right, Jaseer.

859
01:07:53.833 --> 01:07:55.625
We must change with the times.

860
01:07:57.750 --> 01:07:59.917
If you take so much time to cut this,

861
01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:02.875
there won't be any money left
to pay you when we sell it.

862
01:08:03.750 --> 01:08:04.625
What are you doing?

863
01:08:04.708 --> 01:08:05.708
Bring them quickly!

864
01:08:05.792 --> 01:08:07.432
What's the purpose
of making these sounds?

865
01:08:08.583 --> 01:08:10.417
How many have you cut, Jaseer?

866
01:08:10.625 --> 01:08:12.292
I'm doing it, sir.
It will be over now.

867
01:08:12.625 --> 01:08:14.625
That's not enough.
Finish the rest too, quickly.

868
01:08:14.708 --> 01:08:17.333
Don't you know
what the market is like right now?

869
01:08:45.542 --> 01:08:46.667
You rascal!

870
01:08:47.208 --> 01:08:48.729
What are you looking at in the mirror?

871
01:08:48.958 --> 01:08:50.083
Admiring your beauty?

872
01:08:50.958 --> 01:08:52.000
Get back to work!

873
01:08:52.667 --> 01:08:53.792
He's admiring his looks!

874
01:08:54.417 --> 01:08:55.458
Idiot!

875
01:09:32.000 --> 01:09:33.333
This beard…

876
01:09:38.208 --> 01:09:39.917
How long has it been?

877
01:09:44.667 --> 01:09:46.458
How many days has it been?

878
01:09:50.167 --> 01:09:52.292
I can't remember anything!

879
01:09:54.750 --> 01:09:55.875
How long…

880
01:10:09.500 --> 01:10:11.833
I can't do this, Mom.

881
01:10:14.583 --> 01:10:17.833
I'm exhausted, Mom…

882
01:10:21.458 --> 01:10:22.708
I'm fed up.

883
01:10:25.583 --> 01:10:27.542
I'm sick and tired.

884
01:10:31.292 --> 01:10:32.458
God…

885
01:10:39.417 --> 01:10:42.417
Why should I call on God?

886
01:10:45.333 --> 01:10:47.250
Why should I pray to God?

887
01:10:50.583 --> 01:10:51.917
If there were a God…

888
01:10:53.625 --> 01:10:57.333
my fate wouldn't be like this.

889
01:12:32.167 --> 01:12:33.167
Brother!

890
01:12:44.500 --> 01:12:45.542
Brother…

891
01:14:02.750 --> 01:14:04.500
Mom!

892
01:14:52.875 --> 01:14:53.917
I need to go.

893
01:14:56.750 --> 01:14:57.792
I must go back.

894
01:14:58.917 --> 01:15:00.458
I don't care even if I die.

895
01:15:03.167 --> 01:15:04.250
I must leave.

896
01:16:11.750 --> 01:16:13.500
Stop there, you dog!

897
01:16:15.792 --> 01:16:16.792
Go!

898
01:17:04.792 --> 01:17:07.250
- You dog!
- Hey…

899
01:17:07.333 --> 01:17:08.333
Stop there, you!

900
01:17:08.417 --> 01:17:11.583
Where do you think you're trying
to escape to, you swine?

901
01:17:11.792 --> 01:17:14.125
Where are you going?
Stay there, you swine!

902
01:17:15.333 --> 01:17:17.875
Are you running away from me?
You dog!

903
01:17:21.542 --> 01:17:24.417
What were you thinking?
I'll teach you a lesson, you dog!

904
01:17:24.708 --> 01:17:25.750
You scoundrel!

905
01:17:25.958 --> 01:17:29.583
I will kill you, you filthy animal!

906
01:17:29.667 --> 01:17:31.458
How dare you run away from me?

907
01:17:31.750 --> 01:17:33.250
Where were you trying to escape to?

908
01:25:30.583 --> 01:25:31.625
Hey!

909
01:26:04.917 --> 01:26:05.917
Who is that?

910
01:26:07.792 --> 01:26:08.792
It's me.

911
01:26:13.083 --> 01:26:14.125
It's me!

912
01:26:22.792 --> 01:26:24.167
Hakim!

913
01:26:24.833 --> 01:26:26.167
Kiddo!

914
01:26:32.875 --> 01:26:33.875
Brother…

915
01:26:34.250 --> 01:26:37.167
I can't believe this!

916
01:26:39.500 --> 01:26:42.542
Only your voice is the same.

917
01:26:43.375 --> 01:26:44.583
You look so different.

918
01:26:46.333 --> 01:26:50.542
Only your voice is the same!

919
01:26:58.792 --> 01:27:00.208
Hakim…

920
01:27:05.083 --> 01:27:07.042
I will die, brother!

921
01:27:07.125 --> 01:27:11.542
I will… die here!

922
01:27:12.583 --> 01:27:14.333
How long has it been?

923
01:27:16.208 --> 01:27:20.417
How many years has it been?

924
01:27:21.208 --> 01:27:23.875
I don't know anything.

925
01:27:25.500 --> 01:27:27.417
I don't know anything!

926
01:27:28.125 --> 01:27:31.458
Come on, brother.
Let's get out of here.

927
01:27:31.542 --> 01:27:33.292
Let's escape from here. Come!

928
01:27:36.667 --> 01:27:38.000
How?

929
01:27:39.708 --> 01:27:41.042
Where to?

930
01:27:42.083 --> 01:27:45.042
I tried so many times!

931
01:27:45.583 --> 01:27:49.208
I tried for so many days!

932
01:27:53.917 --> 01:27:57.167
It's been only a few days
since I came here.

933
01:27:57.458 --> 01:28:01.708
I was made to work
at several places before that.

934
01:28:02.167 --> 01:28:03.750
They tortured me!

935
01:28:07.750 --> 01:28:09.167
That's my Kafeel.

936
01:28:09.417 --> 01:28:10.500
I'm leaving.

937
01:28:10.917 --> 01:28:12.458
I'm not afraid of dying now.

938
01:28:12.542 --> 01:28:13.684
- I could see you, right?
- Hakim…

939
01:28:13.708 --> 01:28:14.708
I was able to see you.

940
01:28:15.625 --> 01:28:16.667
I'm leaving.

941
01:28:22.208 --> 01:28:23.458
Go back, brother!

942
01:28:23.625 --> 01:28:24.708
Don't let him spot you!

943
01:29:01.125 --> 01:29:02.125
Brother!

944
01:29:13.292 --> 01:29:15.167
Brother! Brother!

945
01:30:40.875 --> 01:30:42.000
What are you doing there?

946
01:30:44.125 --> 01:30:46.000
- I'm taking a dump.
- Taking a dump?

947
01:30:47.000 --> 01:30:48.292
Where are you taking a dump?

948
01:30:49.167 --> 01:30:50.167
Listen!

949
01:30:50.500 --> 01:30:54.542
Take the camels back to the Masara
before the sandstorm arrives.

950
01:30:55.292 --> 01:31:00.000
I'm telling you, take the camels
back to the Masara before sunset.

951
01:31:29.958 --> 01:31:33.250
<i>Brother, I was severely beaten that day.</i>

952
01:31:33.542 --> 01:31:36.292
<i>That's alright.
I'm happy that I was able to meet you.</i>

953
01:31:36.667 --> 01:31:39.750
<i>I've only been working here
for a few days.</i>

954
01:31:40.083 --> 01:31:42.250
<i>There's an African man
who works with me here.</i>

955
01:31:42.625 --> 01:31:44.625
<i>He has worked here earlier as well.</i>

956
01:31:44.958 --> 01:31:48.125
<i>He's very familiar with most
of the routes and locations here.</i>

957
01:31:48.750 --> 01:31:51.375
<i>If he helps us, we can escape.</i>

958
01:31:51.750 --> 01:31:55.208
<i>I feel like he has been sent to us
like Allah sent Prophet Moses.</i>

959
01:31:55.708 --> 01:31:57.458
<i>Let's pray to the Almighty.</i>

960
01:32:51.250 --> 01:32:52.625
Hakim, come!

961
01:32:55.458 --> 01:32:56.583
Quick!

962
01:33:04.875 --> 01:33:07.792
Look! That's your friend's Masara.

963
01:33:25.042 --> 01:33:26.167
Come on!

964
01:33:51.500 --> 01:33:55.292
<i>O Almighty, O Gracious</i>

965
01:33:55.417 --> 01:33:59.208
<i>O Almighty, O Merciful</i>

966
01:34:02.333 --> 01:34:06.583
<i>O Almighty, O Gracious</i>

967
01:34:06.708 --> 01:34:10.417
<i>O Almighty, O Merciful</i>

968
01:34:12.875 --> 01:34:16.875
<i>How far away are You?</i>

969
01:34:17.125 --> 01:34:20.625
<i>How far away are You?</i>

970
01:34:22.333 --> 01:34:26.083
<i>The sparrow's glance</i>

971
01:34:26.625 --> 01:34:30.458
<i>Talk and smile</i>

972
01:34:30.875 --> 01:34:33.792
<i>Those dimples lovely and beguile</i>

973
01:34:33.958 --> 01:34:38.917
<i>That love's lantern, casting a glow</i>

974
01:34:39.542 --> 01:34:45.583
<i>Illuminates my soul's chambers
Dark and low</i>

975
01:34:47.750 --> 01:34:54.583
<i>At the tips of those eyes, tears part…</i>

976
01:35:06.625 --> 01:35:07.708
It's okay.

977
01:35:08.417 --> 01:35:09.417
Hakim!

978
01:35:10.667 --> 01:35:11.750
What is it?

979
01:35:11.958 --> 01:35:13.000
Nothing, brother.

980
01:35:13.375 --> 01:35:16.125
- What happened?
- This is Khadiri.

981
01:35:20.875 --> 01:35:22.042
Peace be upon you!

982
01:35:23.583 --> 01:35:24.750
Ibrahim Khadiri.

983
01:35:26.708 --> 01:35:27.792
How are you doing?

984
01:35:29.083 --> 01:35:31.250
- Are you Hakim's friend?
- Yes.

985
01:35:31.708 --> 01:35:34.792
Brother, Khadiri knows all the places
and routes here very well.

986
01:35:35.042 --> 01:35:36.250
He's from Africa.

987
01:35:38.083 --> 01:35:41.125
Escaping from the Kafeel
is quite difficult.

988
01:35:42.250 --> 01:35:44.833
But the Kafeel's daughter's
wedding is coming up.

989
01:35:45.375 --> 01:35:46.976
When all the Kafeels go
for the wedding celebrations,

990
01:35:47.000 --> 01:35:48.440
it might give us a window to escape.

991
01:35:48.708 --> 01:35:49.792
May God help us.

992
01:35:51.292 --> 01:35:53.333
- Hakim…
- Tell him.

993
01:35:53.667 --> 01:35:57.000
Brother, our chief Kafeel's daughter's
wedding is coming up in a few days.

994
01:35:57.208 --> 01:36:01.625
By God's grace, if they leave this place
on that day, we can make our escape.

995
01:36:08.292 --> 01:36:10.292
Didn't you understand
what I said, brother?

996
01:36:12.917 --> 01:36:14.083
How?

997
01:36:18.000 --> 01:36:19.042
So…

998
01:36:20.000 --> 01:36:21.125
far away.

999
01:36:21.333 --> 01:36:22.500
Can we do it?

1000
01:36:23.917 --> 01:36:26.792
Why are you saying that, brother?

1001
01:36:29.875 --> 01:36:32.000
If we can't escape, we'll die together.

1002
01:36:32.292 --> 01:36:34.167
Should we stay here and suffer?

1003
01:36:34.500 --> 01:36:36.500
- Hakim…
- I can't do this anymore.

1004
01:36:43.167 --> 01:36:44.167
Let's go!

1005
01:36:44.750 --> 01:36:47.500
Let's leave this place somehow.

1006
01:36:49.083 --> 01:36:50.583
Hey, don't cry.

1007
01:36:51.500 --> 01:36:52.583
Don't cry.

1008
01:36:53.125 --> 01:36:54.417
Come on, let's go.

1009
01:36:55.792 --> 01:36:57.708
See you!
God willing!

1010
01:36:58.042 --> 01:37:00.417
Brother, everything will be alright.

1011
01:37:00.667 --> 01:37:01.917
Pray to God.

1012
01:37:28.833 --> 01:37:32.000
Dear friends!
I greatly appreciate your presence.

1013
01:37:32.375 --> 01:37:34.000
May God bless you!

1014
01:37:34.958 --> 01:37:36.167
May God bless you!

1015
01:37:41.042 --> 01:37:43.792
May God bless you all.

1016
01:37:54.125 --> 01:37:57.250
- You are most welcome.
- Thank you.

1017
01:37:57.417 --> 01:38:01.458
- I'm pleased to see you.
- Thank you.

1018
01:38:01.542 --> 01:38:03.833
Welcome! Please come.

1019
01:38:14.000 --> 01:38:15.125
Hey, Hindi!

1020
01:38:15.958 --> 01:38:17.000
You're sitting here?

1021
01:38:19.542 --> 01:38:20.542
Take this.

1022
01:38:21.375 --> 01:38:22.500
Here, have some meat.

1023
01:38:23.000 --> 01:38:25.375
Eat it, for the special occasion
of my daughter's wedding.

1024
01:38:26.000 --> 01:38:29.000
God willing! On the wedding day,
we will serve you biryani.

1025
01:39:04.917 --> 01:39:05.958
Allah!

1026
01:39:06.292 --> 01:39:07.500
You are right!

1027
01:39:10.417 --> 01:39:11.458
What's with you?

1028
01:39:12.333 --> 01:39:14.292
Go and unload the goods from the vehicle.

1029
01:39:14.417 --> 01:39:16.542
I have to go to the wedding. Quick!

1030
01:39:16.708 --> 01:39:17.708
Alright.

1031
01:39:19.500 --> 01:39:20.820
Are you peeking at me from there?

1032
01:39:22.625 --> 01:39:23.917
That's an awesome speaker!

1033
01:39:24.917 --> 01:39:26.500
It has such great bass!

1034
01:39:27.792 --> 01:39:29.000
Unload it quickly.

1035
01:39:30.375 --> 01:39:32.542
He has to go to the wedding.

1036
01:39:38.583 --> 01:39:39.833
Oh, God!

1037
01:39:40.708 --> 01:39:42.083
I'll die in this heat.

1038
01:39:42.833 --> 01:39:43.958
Hey!

1039
01:39:49.542 --> 01:39:51.167
Hey! Don't worry.

1040
01:39:51.250 --> 01:39:53.210
You'll be getting
some of the wedding biryani too.

1041
01:39:54.917 --> 01:39:56.250
- Sir!
- Yes!

1042
01:39:56.333 --> 01:39:58.083
I have unloaded the goods.
I'm leaving.

1043
01:39:58.792 --> 01:40:01.333
Come tomorrow. I'll get you
some biryani from the wedding feast.

1044
01:40:01.917 --> 01:40:03.708
Hey, you! Hindi!
Come on!

1045
01:40:04.375 --> 01:40:05.458
Here.

1046
01:40:05.750 --> 01:40:07.583
Take it.
This is your dinner for tonight.

1047
