1571
02:42:27.000 --> 02:42:29.833
- I'll show you what I can do!
- Don't take me back!

1572
02:42:30.167 --> 02:42:32.643
- Please don't take me back there!
- I will teach you a lesson!

1573
02:42:32.667 --> 02:42:34.667
Don't take me back there!

1574
02:42:34.750 --> 02:42:36.667
I'll show you what I can do!

1575
02:42:37.917 --> 02:42:39.875
I will teach you a lesson!

1576
02:42:39.958 --> 02:42:41.250
Don't hit me!

1577
02:43:38.958 --> 02:43:40.250
So, you got away?

1578
02:43:41.167 --> 02:43:44.327
If you were really under my sponsorship,
I'd have hauled you back to the Masara.

1579
02:43:49.583 --> 02:43:53.000
It's so hot in here.

1580
02:43:53.875 --> 02:43:56.625
Najeeb, he was not your actual sponsor.

1581
02:43:57.042 --> 02:43:59.417
If he was, he would've dragged
you back to the Masara now.

1582
02:44:00.167 --> 02:44:02.807
Your visa was sponsored by someone else,
but this man abducted you.

1583
02:44:06.125 --> 02:44:09.167
He was working under this Arab.

1584
02:44:09.833 --> 02:44:11.042
So unfortunate!

1585
02:44:42.167 --> 02:44:46.167
ALL THE LIVES WE'VE NEVER EXPERIENCED
ARE JUST STORIES FOR US

1586
02:44:54.250 --> 02:44:57.083
<i>The three months I spent in jail</i>

1587
02:44:57.667 --> 02:44:59.833
<i>felt longer than the three years
I spent in the desert.</i>

1588
02:45:00.708 --> 02:45:03.083
<i>Since I began to feel hopeful
about returning home,</i>

1589
02:45:03.583 --> 02:45:05.250
<i>I haven't slept at all.</i>

1590
02:45:05.750 --> 02:45:08.083
<i>It was a long wait for the out-pass.</i>

1591
02:45:08.833 --> 02:45:12.625
<i>At the airport,
amidst the crowd awaiting expats</i>

1592
02:45:13.042 --> 02:45:17.167
<i>with large suitcases filled with perfumes,
tape recorders, and televisions,</i>

1593
02:45:17.542 --> 02:45:20.582
<i>my son and Sainu will be waiting for me.
All that remains for me to give them</i>

1594
02:45:21.708 --> 02:45:24.125
<i>is the time I have left in my life.</i>

1595
02:45:26.292 --> 02:45:27.583
THIS IS NOT JUST NAJEEB'S STORY.

1596
02:45:27.708 --> 02:45:30.708
IT IS THE GRIEF OF MANY THOUSANDS
WHO HAVE LOST THEIR LIVES IN THE DESERT

1597
02:45:30.833 --> 02:45:32.309
LEAVING THEIR COUNTRY AND HOME
TO SURVIVE.

1598
02:45:32.333 --> 02:45:36.250
<i>O Almighty, O Gracious</i>

1599
02:45:36.417 --> 02:45:39.875
<i>O Almighty, O Merciful</i>
